  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Chevron Usa received $339M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Chevron Usa won 85 awards with an average award size of $4M, and obligations were up 46.7% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows growing activity from FY21 through FY26: FY21 was $55.8M, FY22 was $116M, FY23 was $180M, FY24 was $132M, FY25 was $231M, and FY26 is $339M. Petroleum Refineries is the dominant NAICS market for Chevron Usa, accounting for $338M of obligations, followed by Other Warehousing and Storage at $1.1M. Current-year totals are partial, and award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables are total contract values rather than obligations. This profile shows where federal dollars are concentrated and how award size and count combine to produce the year-to-date total. Use the fiscal-year series and NAICS breakdown to track concentration and recent momentum in government work for Chevron Usa.",
